    "result_text": "All tests pass. `BUILD SUCCESS` with 0 failures/errors across the full suite.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a `selfLink` field to the Owner API response equal to `/api/owners/` followed by the owner id.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `selfLink` (readOnly string) property to the `Owner` response schema. This regenerates `OwnerDto` with `getSelfLink`/`setSelfLink`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added one `@Mapping(target = \"selfLink\", expression = \"java(\\\"/api/owners/\\\" + owner.getId())\")` line to `toOwnerDto`.\n\n**Why the mapper (not the responders):** `selfLink` is purely derived from `owner.getId()`, which the mapper already has \u2014 so it belongs alongside the ~15 other derived DTO fields (displayName, salutation, customerCode, \u2026) rather than being duplicated in each responder. This gives it to every response path (GET single, list, and 201 Created) for free with a single source of truth. `bulkSignupWarning` stays in the responders only because it needs the `OwnerRepository`, which the mapper doesn't have \u2014 that constraint doesn't apply here, so no reason to copy the pattern.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsSelfLink` passes, and the full suite remains green.",
